            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery arising as a terminal extension of the circumflex artery (a rare coronary artery anomaly).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>737-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A single coronary artery is a very rare type of coronary artery anomaly that may present in various forms. A patient is presented in whom the right coronary artery coursed as the terminal branch of the left circumflex artery. This is the second case of this anomaly in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
